error[SC0307]: the declarations of `g` disagree about nullability
   ╭─[ declarations_that_disagree_between_nullable_and_nothing_are_refused.c:1:14 ]
   │
 1 │ void g(int * _Nullable p);
   │              ────┬────  
   │                  ╰────── one declaration says `_Nullable` here
 2 │ void g(int *p);
   │      ┬  
   │      ╰── this declaration says nothing
───╯
  = note: every declaration of a function has to agree about its nullability specifiers, because a caller is checked against the declaration it sees
